    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner resource. It returns `true` when any of the three conditions hold, otherwise `false`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `riskFlag` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.setRiskFlag(...)`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Marked `riskFlag` as `ignore = true` on `toOwnerDto`, consistent with the other context-derived warning flags (`bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`) that are set in the controller rather than from a single `Owner` field.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - `riskFlag(Owner)` combining the three conditions with OR.\n   - `overSoftCityCapacity(city)` \u2014 city holds `SOFT_CITY_CAPACITY` (40) or more owners, counted the same way as the existing hard 50-owner limit.\n   - `isDisposableAdjacentEmailDomain(email)` \u2014 the email's domain equals a disposable domain or is a subdomain of one. This is intentionally broader than the existing `isDisposableEmailDomain` (which rejects *exact* disposable domains at create time with 400): a stored owner sitting just off the blocklist gets flagged for review rather than rejected.\n   - Set `ownerDto.setRiskFlag(...)` in all three response paths (create, GET, and the idempotent-replay path).\n\n**Interpretation notes** (the prompt was the only spec; I chose the reading most consistent with existing code):\n- *possible duplicate* \u2192 `possibleDuplicateOf != null` (the same signal as the existing `possibleDuplicate` field).\n- *disposable-adjacent* \u2192 on-or-adjacent-to the disposable blocklist (exact match or subdomain), since exact matches are already rejected at create so a distinct softer notion is needed.\n- *over soft capacity* \u2192 \u2265 40 owners in the city (soft threshold below the hard 50 limit; aligns with the existing capacity-warning band's lower bound and also covers a full city of 50).\n\nThe one provided acceptance test (`riskFlag` false for a normal owner) passes, and nothing else regressed.",
